Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||10-05-2000||11:01 AM||||Ok, I'm completely conviced this site is a hoax..<P>I'm reading an essay on the page about human brains and consciousness.. and there are several blantantly obvious errors, common misconceptions, etc. that a neurosurgeon would NOT make.. plus all of the "clients" look like models, both before and after... who'd have a professional photo taken before a brain transplant? the before shots should look like mugshots, if it were real.. and shouldn't the after shots have some scarring around the upper forehead? it'd take a lot of cosmetic surgery to erase evidence of surgery that extreme..<P>I pretty much guessed it was a hoax all along (as indicated by my initial response.. hehe) but since I think this stuff is cool, I was willing to give it a chance and check out the site.. even if just for a laugh..<P>and "The heads do not respond." line was well worth it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||13
